name o4-10-two-v-two-1
timeout 600

# CAMPAIGN O4, SORTIE 10 OF 10 — THE WHOLE CAMPAIGN ONE LEVEL UP.
# doc/campaigns/o4-gaf-mig29g-dact.md mission 10. Two against two, mixed doctrines, real weather, and
# the only sortie of the ten whose verdict is `kill team` rather than `kill unit`.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: the nine sorties before this one measure two aircraft. Does the answer
# survive a second aircraft a side — and what does the MiG-29's missing cooperative channel cost when
# it does? None of that asymmetry is mission data; it is what the two modules ARE
# (doc/formation.md §7, doc/modules/mig29/datalink-gci.md §5.1):
#   channel  F-16: MIDS-LVT — every member transmits its own fix, its flight position and a target
#            POINT with a "my round still needs me" bit, once a second. MiG-29: NOTHING. The 9-12 has
#            no cooperative terminal; its picture comes from a ground controller over voice, and a
#            controller is not a track list.
#   sort     F-16: computed per tick from the shared picture and deconflicted by the lead's claim.
#            MiG-29: the briefed CONTRACT (`set brief_sort left`), agreed before takeoff and applied by
#            each pilot to the picture he personally has. Dynamic, and blind.
#   cover    the rule that keeps ONE member of a flight free is the same on both sides; its PRICE is
#            not. [MESS, pair-2v2-asym.fbm] an AIM-120 binds its shooter for 0.3 s, an R-27R for
#            17.3 s — a factor of 58 — and the MiG has no channel on which "my leader is bound" could
#            travel, so its measured deferral is 0 s BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by choice.
#   sort quality, measured on the same instrument: cooperative 0.962 against briefed contract 0.750 —
#            one in four contract shooters is doubled up on a target a mate already has.
#
# THE WEATHER IS THE CAMPAIGN'S OWN FIXTURE, as the spec's mission table asks. o4-08-weather.fbm has
# already measured what it does and does not do on this block, so it enters here as a known quantity
# rather than as a second experiment: it blinds the eye (`vis MASKED`, transmittance 0.011) and moves
# every trajectory through 11.2 m/s of wind at the fight's own level, and neither of those two channels
# has a consumer in pilot/FBPilot.
#
# THE GROUND: two range hulks as in every other sortie of the campaign, plus a hardened target at the
# east end — the 2 x target_soft + 1 x target_hard the spec's cast table asks for. Nothing in O4 carries
# an air-to-ground weapon (the MiG-29 module cannot fly `set task attack` at all, gap C9), so the ground
# is what campaign rule 3 says it is: the reason each side is where it is, and not a target set. The
# campaign carries `ground` all the same, and the campaign report says plainly that it carries nothing.
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-29): exit 3, FOUR ARRIVALS AND NO KILL. Two AIM-120 at 5.09 m and 6.19 m — both on
# `fulcrum9`, so the cooperative sort did NOT split the pair's rounds — an R-27R at 12.20 m against a
# 13.8 m fuze, and an R-73 at 2.64 m against the F-16's 2.32 m kill radius. The channel asymmetry shows
# up as NOISE rather than as advantage: 74 `flight SORT_ASSIGN` lines, `flt_switch` 52 and 19 on the
# cooperative pair against 2 and 1 on the contract pair, and 0 `COVER_DEFER` on either side. That is the
# first measurement in the tree saying the cooperative channel can be busier than the briefed contract
# without being better on the geometry it is measured on, and it belongs beside doc/formation.md's
# 0.962-against-0.750 sort quality rather than instead of it.
#
# READING RULE: the verdict is the TELEMETRY and the `kill team` outcome together. Read `flt_src`
# (1 = cooperative, 2 = contract), `flt_both_s` (seconds two flight-mates were bound at once),
# `flt_defer_s` (seconds a trigger was held to keep the cover) and `flt_exposed_s`, then the per-jet
# eng_* debriefing and the DETONATION lines. exit 3 (TIMEOUT) is the expected shape — a `kill team`
# objective needs BOTH opponents down — and it is not a failure. exit 2 would be a defect.

wx fixture wx-2026-07-27T00Z.wxb

unit viper9
  team friendly
  flight viper 1
  module f16
  spawn 55.20000 12.72600 8000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink on                             # the cooperative half of the asymmetry
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 55.20000 14.60000 8000 450
  objective kill team hostile
  objective survive

